  "result": "I changed the paging so that entries recorded at the same moment are no longer skipped. I haven't run the test suite or a page-by-page walk.\n\nThe fault was in `keysetPredicate` in `src/server/repositories/_paging.ts`. It resumed a page with only `sortColumn < cursor.sortValue`, so after a page boundary it dropped every row that shared the last row's timestamp. That is why bulk imports and assignment bursts lost entries while gradually created ones paged correctly.\n\nIt now resumes with `sortColumn < v OR (sortColumn = v AND id < cursorId)`. That matches the `ORDER BY <sort> DESC, id DESC` the listings already use.\n\nAll the cursor-paged lists share this helper. Each one filters on `orgId` separately, and the new condition sits alongside that filter. I didn't read each repository's filters to confirm they all include it.\n\nThe paging code also caps page size at 100 (`probeLimit` and `toPage`). I left that as it is.",
